{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01FPVDntPXv62UfLvP5vMHi9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  核心 \"universal failure mode\" 叙事被全面拒绝。Reviewer 1 引用 RateQuant Appendix M 论证 compounding 是已知现象，\n  Reviewer 2 指出 n=8 上 \"universal\" 不成立且 1.07× mild cases 属噪声，Reviewer 3 将 cardinality constraint\n  定性为 \"grid search over one hyperparameter\"。7/8 negative 被解读为方法无价值的铁证。论文需彻底重构为\n  \"When Does Per-Head KV Cache Quantization Help? A Systematic Empirical Study\"——放弃 discovery + fix 叙事，\n  转向 systematic benchmark + taxonomy + diagnostic 的 resource contribution framing。Compounding 和 constraint\n  降级为 Section 4 支撑分析，不再作为核心贡献。Title 改为 \"Per-Head KV Cache Quantization: When It Helps,\n  When It Hurts, and How to Tell\"。需补充 3+ 额外架构、更多压缩比 sweep、更多 baseline 对比（KIVI/GEAR）。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"L0 exclusion removal\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_001\"\n    description: \"移除 L0 exclusion constraint，仅保留 max_2bit=8，验证 solver 自动发现 L0 sensitivity\"\n    expected_results:\n      solver_assigns_8bit_to_L0: true\n      ppl_without_l0_exclusion: 10.91\n      ppl_with_l0_exclusion: 10.91\n      delta: 0.0\n      l0_heads_bit_assignment: \"8-bit (all 4 L0 heads)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Solver 确实自动将 L0 heads 分配到 8-bit——但 reviewer 将此解读为 \"profiler works as expected,\n      this is not a finding\"。R2 评论：\"Of course a sensitivity-based allocator assigns high bits to\n      the most sensitive heads. This is the expected behavior of ANY profiling-based method, not a\n      contribution.\" R3 补充：\"This just shows the profiler is not broken — it would be alarming if\n      it DIDN'T assign 8-bit to L0.\" 在 worst 档下，这个实验从 \"solver discovers structure\" 的正面叙事\n      变成 \"trivially expected behavior\" 的无贡献证据。新 framing 下降级为 methodology validation\n      footnote。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"L0 exclusion ablation (Qwen2.5-7B, budget=0.25)\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"With L0 exclusion\", 10.91, \"{8:4, 4:100, 2:8}\", 0.25]\n          - [\"Without L0 exclusion\", 10.91, \"{8:4, 4:100, 2:8}\", 0.25]\n          - [\"Uniform 4-bit\", 15.45, \"all 4-bit\", 0.25]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"无独立 figure——在新 framing 下此实验不值得单独可视化\"\n    analysis: >\n      Reviewer 视角：结果 trivially correct，不构成任何贡献。在重构后的论文中仅作为 §3 methodology\n      的一句话验证（\"We verify that the sensitivity-based allocator automatically assigns higher\n      bit-widths to the most sensitive heads without manual exclusion rules\"），不列为 finding。\n\n  - name: \"Llama-3.1-8B full pipeline\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_002\"\n    description: \"在 Llama-3.1-8B (GQA 4:1) 上复制完整 pipeline，测试跨架构泛化\"\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_ppl_bf16: 8.09\n      uniform_4bit_ppl: 8.47\n      mckp_constrained_ppl: 8.45\n      delta_vs_uniform: +0.2%\n      delta_vs_uniform_ppl: -0.02\n      unconstrained_degradation_ratio: 1.07\n      natural_2bit_count: 2\n      concentration: 0.57\n      distribution_shape: \"Spike\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      MCKP 仅比 uniform 好 0.02 PPL——reviewer 认为这在 calibration noise 范围内（multi-seed std=0.065\n      on Qwen，Llama 的 0.02 差距更小）。R1：\"A 0.2% improvement is statistically indistinguishable\n      from noise without multi-seed confidence intervals on Llama.\" R2 将 1.07× unconstrained\n      degradation 定性为噪声：\"1.07× could easily be explained by evaluation variance — you need\n      to show this is significantly different from 1.0.\" 在 worst 档下，Llama 成为 \"non-uniform\n      allocation is pointless on this architecture\" 的直接证据，而 reviewer 进一步推论：\"If profiling\n      + MCKP + constraint adds complexity for zero benefit on 7/8 models, the method has negative\n      expected value.\" 新 framing 下 Llama 是 \"when it doesn't help\" 的 case study，支撑 systematic\n      coverage 贡献。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Llama-3.1-8B allocation comparison (budget=0.25)\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"BF16 baseline\", 8.09, \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Uniform 4-bit\", 8.47, \"all 4-bit\", 0.25]\n          - [\"MCKP constrained (k=2)\", 8.45, \"{2:2, 4:253, 8:1}\", 0.25]\n          - [\"MCKP unconstrained\", 8.63, \"{2:12, 4:...}\", 0.25]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Llama sensitivity heatmap showing spike pattern (L2H5 dominant, t₁/t₅=0.85)\"\n    analysis: >\n      在 worst framing 下，Llama 的 negative result 强化 reviewer 论点：per-head allocation 对大多数\n      架构无价值。但在重构后的 \"systematic study\" framing 下，Llama 是 boundary condition case\n      (concentration=0.57, just above 0.50 threshold, but t₁/t₅=0.85 violates second criterion)，\n      证明 diagnostic 的 joint condition 比单一 threshold 更准确。\n\n  - name: \"Mistral-7B-v0.3 full pipeline\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003\"\n    description: \"在 Mistral-7B-v0.3 上复制完整 pipeline\"\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_ppl_bf16: 7.035\n      uniform_4bit_ppl: 7.131\n      mckp_constrained_ppl: 7.165\n      delta_vs_uniform: -0.4%\n      delta_vs_uniform_ppl: -0.034\n      unconstrained_degradation_ratio: 1.08\n      concentration: 0.22\n      distribution_shape: \"Flat\"\n      k_ablation_monotonic: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      MCKP 比 uniform 4-bit 差 0.034 PPL——non-uniform allocation 在 Mistral 上 actively harmful。\n      R3 引用此结果：\"Your method HURTS performance on Mistral. The profiler reports near-zero\n      sensitivity differences, meaning your entire profiling pipeline produces zero signal on this\n      architecture. This is not 'honest negative result' — it's evidence the method doesn't\n      generalize.\" k ablation 单调递增进一步证实：每增加一个 2-bit head 都损害质量，最优 k=0 即\n      uniform 4-bit。Reviewer 将 1.08× unconstrained 归为 noise，与 Llama 1.07× 一起构成 \"mild\n      cases are noise\" 的论据。新 framing 下 Mistral 是 \"profiler zero-signal\" 的典型 case，支撑\n      \"when to skip profiling\" 的 diagnostic 贡献。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Mistral-7B-v0.3 k ablation (budget=0.25)\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"k=0 (uniform)\", 7.131, 0, 256, \"optimal\"]\n          - [\"k=4\", 7.165, 4, 252, \"best constrained\"]\n          - [\"k=8\", 7.200, 8, 247, \"\"]\n          - [\"k=16\", 7.311, 16, 238, \"\"]\n          - [\"k=18\", 7.323, 18, 235, \"worst\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Mistral k-PPL curve: 单调递增，无 U-shape，证实 zero-signal profiler\"\n    analysis: >\n      Mistral 是 reviewer 攻击 universality claim 的最强武器。Monotonic k-PPL 证明没有任何 k 值能\n      让 non-uniform 优于 uniform。在重构论文中，Mistral 与 Gemma-2 一起构成 \"Flat distribution:\n      skip profiling\" 的 taxonomy 类别。\n\n  - name: \"Compounding effect sweep\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: \"在 Qwen2.5-7B 上 sweep max_2bit 从 0 到 112，绘制 compounding threshold\"\n    expected_results:\n      k0_ppl: 9.81\n      k8_ppl: 10.05\n      k16_ppl: 10.42\n      k32_ppl: 11.60\n      k64_ppl: 23.22\n      k112_ppl: ~98.75\n      compounding_onset_k: ~32\n      max_compounding_ratio: 10.07\n      u_shape: true\n      optimal_k: 8\n    result_rationale: >\n      Reviewer 承认 PPL 随 k 增加而上升，但拒绝将此称为 \"discovery\"。R1 引用 RateQuant Appendix M：\n      \"Zhang et al. (2024) explicitly discuss that quantization errors compound when multiple\n      heads are simultaneously quantized to low bit-widths. Your sweep merely quantifies a known\n      phenomenon.\" R2 补充：\"This is the expected behavior of any lossy compression — more aggressive\n      compression leads to more degradation. The curve shape is unsurprising.\" R3 指出 U-shape\n      仅在 Qwen 上出现：\"Llama shows flat, Mistral shows monotonic increase. The U-shape is a\n      Qwen-specific artifact, not a universal phenomenon.\" 在 worst 档下，compounding sweep 从\n      \"principled motivation for constraint\" 降级为 \"expected compression behavior on one model\"。\n      新 framing 下放入 §4 \"Analysis of allocation failures\" 作为 supporting evidence。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Qwen2.5-7B compounding sweep (budget=0.25, hires profiles)\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"k=0\", 9.81, \"baseline (all 4-bit+)\", 1.00]\n          - [\"k=8\", 10.05, \"constraint threshold\", 1.02]\n          - [\"k=16\", 10.42, \"\", 1.06]\n          - [\"k=32\", 11.60, \"onset of rapid degradation\", 1.18]\n          - [\"k=64\", 23.22, \"catastrophic\", 2.37]\n          - [\"k=96\", ~65, \"\", ~6.6]\n          - [\"k=112 (unconstrained)\", ~98.75, \"\", ~10.07]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Three-panel compounding curve: Qwen (U-shape), Llama (flat then cliff), Mistral (monotonic). Reviewer 会指出三个模型行为完全不同，否定 'universal' 描述\"\n    analysis: >\n      跨架构 compounding sweep 结果实际上 undermines universality：Qwen U-shape (k*=8)，Llama\n      flat-then-cliff (k*=0 即 uniform)，Mistral monotonic (k*=0)。Reviewer 论证：compounding\n      behavior 是架构特异性的，不存在 universal threshold。新 framing 下这成为 taxonomy 的支撑\n      ——不同 distribution shape 对应不同 compounding pattern。\n\n  - name: \"Budget sweep\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: \"在 Qwen2.5-7B 上测试 2×/4×/8× 压缩比下的 constrained MCKP\"\n    expected_results:\n      budget_0.5_mckp_ppl: ~9.85\n      budget_0.5_uniform_ppl: ~10.2\n      budget_0.5_delta: +3.4%\n      budget_0.25_mckp_ppl: 10.91\n      budget_0.25_uniform_ppl: 15.45\n      budget_0.25_delta: +29.4%\n      budget_0.125_mckp_ppl: ~57.6\n      budget_0.125_uniform_2bit_ppl: ~2644\n      budget_0.125_delta: \">45×\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      R2：\"The benefit at 2× compression is marginal (3.4%), and 8× compression is unrealistic\n      for deployment — nobody runs 2-bit KV cache in production. The only interesting data point\n      is 4× where you get 29% on ONE model. This is a single-model, single-compression-ratio\n      result dressed up as a general finding.\" R1 补充：\"At aggressive compression, ANY\n      non-uniform scheme will beat uniform 2-bit — this is trivially true and not a contribution.\n      The interesting regime is moderate compression where your method fails on 7/8 models.\"\n      在 worst 档下，budget sweep 被 reviewer 框定为：mild compression → trivial gain，\n      moderate compression → works on 1/8 only，aggressive compression → trivially expected。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Qwen2.5-7B budget sweep\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"2× (0.50)\", 9.85, 10.2, \"+3.4%\"]\n          - [\"4× (0.25)\", 10.91, 15.45, \"+29.4%\"]\n          - [\"8× (0.125)\", 57.6, 2644, \">45×\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Budget vs PPL recovery curve. Reviewer 会标注 4× 是唯一 'interesting' 区间且仅 Qwen 有效\"\n    analysis: >\n      Budget sweep 在新 framing 下成为 \"compression ratio analysis\" section 的核心——展示\n      benefit 何时出现、何时消失。但 reviewer 拒绝将 aggressive compression 结果计入贡献\n      （trivially expected），将 moderate compression 限定为 n=1 evidence。\n\n  - name: \"High-resolution profiling\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: \"64seq × 2048tok hires profiling on Qwen2.5-7B，测试更精细 profiling 是否改善分配\"\n    expected_results:\n      hires_mckp_ppl: 10.91\n      lowres_mckp_ppl: 11.23\n      improvement_ppl: 0.32\n      hires_nonzero_2bit: 100\n      lowres_nonzero_2bit: 37\n      profiling_time_min: 65.5\n      allocation_diff_count: 8\n    result_rationale: >\n      Hires 确实改善了 0.32 PPL（11.23→10.91），但 R3 攻击 profiling cost：\"65 minutes of GPU\n      time for 0.32 PPL improvement on a 7B model — at this cost, you could simply run the model\n      in fp16. The profiling overhead negates any memory savings for realistic deployment\n      scenarios.\" R1 指出 hires 仅改变了 8/112 heads 的分配：\"The low-resolution profile already\n      gets the constraint right (k=8). The hires improvement is marginal fine-tuning within the\n      feasible set, not a qualitative change.\" 在 worst 档下，hires profiling 被视为 diminishing\n      returns 的证据——大部分 benefit 来自 constraint（lowres constrained 已优于 uniform），\n      profiling resolution 是次要因素。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Profiling resolution comparison (Qwen2.5-7B, k=8)\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Low-res (16×512)\", 11.23, 37, \"~5 min\"]\n          - [\"High-res (64×2048)\", 10.91, 100, \"65.5 min\"]\n          - [\"Uniform 4-bit\", 15.45, \"—\", \"0 min\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Per-head delta heatmap at hires vs lowres. Reviewer 会注意 65 min profiling cost\"\n    analysis: >\n      新 framing 下 profiling resolution 成为 \"practitioner guide\" 的一部分：低分辨率已足够\n      判断是否值得 non-uniform (diagnostic)，高分辨率仅在确认 Spread 模型后才值得投入。\n      但 reviewer 质疑任何 profiling 的 ROI。\n\n  - name: \"C4 cross-dataset evaluation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: \"用 C4 数据集评估 Qwen2.5-7B，验证结果非 WikiText-2 特异性\"\n    expected_results:\n      c4_cal_wt2_eval_mckp_ppl: 11.29\n      c4_cal_wt2_eval_uniform_ppl: 15.45\n      allocation_agreement_c4_vs_wt2: 0.964\n      agreement_heads: \"108/112\"\n      cross_domain_wt2_to_c4_mckp_ppl: 20.56\n      cross_domain_wt2_to_c4_uniform_ppl: 35.42\n    result_rationale: >\n      R2：\"Cross-dataset agreement of 96.4% is expected — head sensitivity is a model property,\n      not a data property. This is a sanity check, not a contribution.\" R1 关注 cross-domain\n      degradation：\"When calibrating on WikiText-2 and evaluating on C4, MCKP PPL is 20.56 vs\n      uniform 35.42 — but both are terrible compared to bf16 baseline of 15.32. The 'benefit'\n      is relative to an already-bad uniform baseline, not absolute quality.\" R3：\"You only test\n      cross-dataset on Qwen, the one model where your method works. Show me cross-dataset\n      results on Llama and Mistral where the method already fails — does it fail worse?\" 实际上\n      Llama/Mistral cross-dataset 也已测试且确认 negative，但 reviewer 将此视为方法无价值的\n      更多证据。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Cross-dataset calibration (Qwen2.5-7B)\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"WTK2-cal → WT2-eval\", 10.91, 15.45, \"+29.4%\"]\n          - [\"C4-cal → WT2-eval\", 11.29, 15.45, \"+27.0%\"]\n          - [\"WT2-cal → C4-eval\", 20.56, 35.42, \"+41.9%\"]\n          - [\"Allocation agreement\", \"96.4%\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Calibration source agreement matrix (仅 Qwen)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cross-dataset robustness 在新 framing 下是 \"benchmark methodology\" 贡献的一部分。但\n      reviewer 认为 96.4% agreement 是 trivially expected，不构成 finding。Llama/Mistral 的\n      cross-dataset negative results 实际上支撑 \"most models don't need profiling\" narrative。\n\n  - name: \"RateQuant greedy comparison\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: \"实现 RateQuant Algorithm 1 在 {2,4,8,16} 上，展示 greedy 在非连续 bit-width 上失败\"\n    expected_results:\n      ratequant_greedy_unconstrained_ppl: 32.45\n      mckp_unconstrained_ppl: 36.92\n      ratequant_greedy_constrained_ppl: 11.23\n      mckp_constrained_ppl: 11.23\n      constrained_delta: 0.0012\n    result_rationale: >\n      R1 (最致命攻击)：\"RateQuant's greedy is designed for consecutive integers {2,...,6} where\n      Prop. 6 guarantees optimality. You're evaluating it on {2,4,8,16} which violates its\n      assumptions — OF COURSE it fails. This is like criticizing a sorting algorithm for not\n      doing matrix multiplication. RateQuant never claimed to work on non-consecutive sets.\"\n      R2：\"Both unconstrained solvers fail (greedy 32.45, MCKP 36.92) — this just confirms that\n      the problem is with unconstrained allocation on {2,4,8,16}, which is a known limitation of\n      hardware-aligned bit-widths, not a novel finding.\" R3：\"Your 'contribution' is adding a\n      single integer parameter k to cap 2-bit heads. This is standard regularization, not a\n      research contribution.\" 在 worst 档下，RateQuant comparison 被完全 invalidated：不公平的\n      comparison + trivial fix = no contribution。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Solver comparison on {2,4,8,16} (Qwen2.5-7B)\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"RateQuant greedy (unconstrained)\", 32.45, \"{2:68, 4:30, 8:4, 16:10}\"]\n          - [\"MCKP (unconstrained)\", 36.92, \"—\"]\n          - [\"RateQuant greedy + k=8\", 11.23, \"{2:8, 4:100, 8:4}\"]\n          - [\"MCKP + k=8\", 11.23, \"{2:8, 4:100, 8:4}\"]\n          - [\"Uniform 4-bit\", 15.45, \"all 4-bit\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Solver equivalence bar chart. Reviewer 会在 caption 加注 'unfair comparison'\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是 worst 档下最致命的 reviewer objection 之一。RateQuant comparison 需要在论文中\n      明确 acknowledge：我们不是说 RateQuant 错了，而是说 hardware-aligned bit-width 引入了\n      RateQuant 未考虑的 failure mode。新 framing 下降级为 \"related work comparison\" 而非\n      核心贡献。\n\n  - name: \"Oracle comparison\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_009\"\n    description: \"Brute-force oracle 在 Qwen2.5-7B 子集上，量化 MCKP 与 oracle 的 gap\"\n    expected_results:\n      mckp_ppl: 10.91\n      max_oracle_gap_ppl: 0.0183\n      avg_oracle_gap_ppl: 0.0046\n      layers_mckp_optimal: \"5/8\"\n      layers_with_gap: 3\n      total_evals: 54\n    result_rationale: >\n      R3：\"MCKP is near-optimal — but this is EXPECTED given that the cardinality constraint\n      reduces the feasible set to where any reasonable solver works. You showed greedy=MCKP\n      already (plan_016). The oracle comparison just confirms the problem is trivially small\n      under the constraint. This reinforces my view that the constraint is doing all the work,\n      and the solver (including your MCKP formulation) is a non-contribution.\" R2：\"If the\n      average gap is 0.005 PPL, the solver doesn't matter. You've proven your own contribution\n      irrelevant.\" 在 worst 档下，oracle comparison 是 double-edged：证明 MCKP near-optimal\n      BUT ALSO 证明问题在 constraint 下退化到 trivial。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"MCKP vs Oracle (Qwen2.5-7B, k=8)\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"MCKP\", 10.91, \"—\"]\n          - [\"Best oracle gap (L1)\", \"+0.018 PPL\", \"2-bit head swap\"]\n          - [\"Avg oracle gap\", \"+0.005 PPL\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Layers MCKP=Oracle\", \"5/8\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Oracle gap 微小 (0.005 PPL) 在 worst framing 下被解读为 \"constrained problem is trivially\n      easy\"——任何 solver 都能解决。新 framing 下移入 appendix 作为 methodology validation。\n\n  - name: \"Cross-domain calibration robustness\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: \"C4 calibration → WikiText-2 评估（及反向），报告 per-head allocation agreement\"\n    expected_results:\n      allocation_agreement_c4_vs_wt2: 0.964\n      agreement_heads: \"108/112\"\n      c4_cal_wt2_eval_mckp_ppl: 11.29\n      cross_domain_delta: 0.034\n    result_rationale: >\n      R2：\"96.4% agreement is a trivial finding. Head sensitivity is a function of model weights,\n      not calibration data — any reasonable calibration set will produce similar profiles. This is\n      a methodology sanity check that belongs in the appendix, not a contribution.\" 在 worst 档下，\n      cross-domain robustness 完全不计入贡献。新 framing 下放入 §3 methodology 的 1-2 句话。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Cross-domain agreement (Qwen2.5-7B)\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"WT2↔C4 agreement\", \"96.4%\", \"108/112 heads\"]\n          - [\"PPL gap (C4-cal vs WT2-cal)\", 0.034, \"noise range\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Sanity check 级别。在重构论文中仅作为 methodology paragraph 的一句验证，不单列。\n\n  - name: \"Head sensitivity visualization\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: \"生成 paper-quality figures: per-head delta heatmap, compounding curve, allocation chart\"\n    expected_results:\n      figures_generated: 3\n      heatmap_shows_l0_dominance: true\n      compounding_curve_u_shape: \"Qwen only\"\n      allocation_chart_constraint_effect: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Visualization 本身不被 reviewer 攻击，但 R1 指出：\"Your heatmap shows that Layer 0 dominance\n      is the only interesting signal in Qwen's sensitivity profile. This is a single architectural\n      quirk, not a generalizable finding. Show me heatmaps for ALL 8 architectures side by side\n      — that would be a systematic study.\" 在 worst 档下，可视化 demand 大幅增加：需要 8 个架构的\n      对比 heatmap + 3 个架构的 compounding curve + taxonomy 分类图。新 framing 下 visualization\n      是 \"systematic benchmark\" 贡献的核心展示方式。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"8-panel heatmap: 每个架构一个 sensitivity heatmap，按 taxonomy (Spread/Spike/Flat) 分组\"\n      - \"Compounding curve comparison: Qwen U-shape vs Llama cliff vs Mistral monotonic\"\n      - \"Sensitivity taxonomy scatter: concentration vs t₁/t₅, 颜色标记 benefit/no-benefit\"\n    analysis: >\n      Reviewer 要求更多可视化来支撑 \"systematic study\" framing。当前 3 张图不够，需扩展到\n      ~8 张以覆盖所有架构的对比分析。\n\n  - name: \"Downstream task evaluation (Qwen)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: \"ARC-C/HellaSwag/PIQA/WinoGrande on Qwen2.5-7B at 4× compression\"\n    expected_results:\n      avg_recovery: 0.728\n      arc_c_delta_pp: +3.16\n      hellaswag_delta_pp: +4.00\n      piqa_delta_pp: +1.25\n      winogrande_delta_pp: +1.97\n      arc_c_mckp: 0.5137\n      arc_c_uniform: 0.4812\n      arc_c_bf16: 0.5290\n    result_rationale: >\n      R2：\"Downstream results confirm that your method works on Qwen — we already knew that from\n      PPL. The question is whether it works on OTHER models, and your own downstream results show\n      it HURTS: Yi -0.77pp, Llama -0.99pp, Mistral -0.48pp. Your method has negative expected\n      value across the tested model population.\" R3：\"72.8% recovery sounds good until you realize\n      it's 72.8% of the gap between uniform 4-bit and bf16 — on a single model. ARC-C shows only\n      +3.16pp which is within single-seed variance range. You provide no confidence intervals for\n      downstream metrics.\" R1 最尖锐：\"4/4 non-Qwen models show downstream degradation. The paper\n      should be titled 'Non-Uniform KV Cache Quantization Hurts Most Models' Downstream, with\n      Qwen as the Exception.'\" 在 worst 档下，downstream eval 成为方法 negative expected value 的\n      证据。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Downstream evaluation across 5 architectures (4×, 0-shot)\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Qwen (Spread)\", \"+1.9pp avg\", \"+3.16 to +4.00pp range\", \"POSITIVE\"]\n          - [\"Yi (Spike)\", \"-0.77pp avg\", \"-3.24pp worst (ARC-C)\", \"NEGATIVE\"]\n          - [\"Llama (Spike)\", \"-0.99pp avg\", \"-2.65pp worst (ARC-C)\", \"NEGATIVE\"]\n          - [\"Mistral (Flat)\", \"-0.48pp avg\", \"-1.19pp worst (ARC-C)\", \"NEGATIVE\"]\n          - [\"Gemma-2 (Flat)\", \"+0.14pp avg\", \"noise range\", \"NEUTRAL\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Per-task heatmap across 5 models: 红色=degradation, 蓝色=improvement. Reviewer 会强调红色占 dominant\"\n    analysis: >\n      跨架构 downstream 数据在 worst 档下是最致命的攻击面。ARC-Challenge 系统性退化\n      (-3.24pp Yi, -2.65pp Llama, -1.19pp Mistral) 被 reviewer 解读为 \"multi-step reasoning\n      tasks are hurt by non-uniform allocation\"。新 framing 必须诚实报告这些 negative 结果\n      并将其作为 \"when not to use non-uniform\" 的核心 evidence。\n\n  - name: \"70B profiling-only\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: \"Qwen2.5-72B profiling only (no full eval)，测试 sensitivity pattern 是否跨 scale\"\n    expected_results:\n      status: killed\n      profiling_completed: false\n      conclusion: \"GPU OOM / timeout\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      R1：\"You claim universality but cannot even run your method on 70B models. The profiling\n      pipeline is too expensive for realistic model sizes. This fundamentally undermines the\n      practical contribution — practitioners work with 70B+ models, not 7B.\" R3：\"Scalability\n      is the elephant in the room. 65 minutes profiling for 7B × 112 heads — extrapolating to\n      72B × 1024+ heads means 10+ hours of GPU time, which is unacceptable.\" 在 worst 档下，\n      70B killed 成为 scalability failure 的直接证据。新 framing 需要 acknowledge scalability\n      limitation explicitly 并提出 efficient profiling 作为 future work。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Killed 状态在 worst 档下被 reviewer 视为论文的重大 gap。\"All results are on 7-14B models —\n      no evidence the method or findings transfer to production-scale models.\" 新 framing 必须\n      在 limitations 明确讨论 scalability。\n\n  - name: \"K/V separation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: \"K/V heads 独立 MCKP allocation vs joint K+V\"\n    expected_results:\n      kv_sep_ppl: 11.22\n      joint_kv_ppl: 10.91\n      uniform_4bit_ppl: 15.45\n      delta_sep_vs_joint: +0.303\n      sep_k_2bit_count: 16\n      sep_v_uniform_4bit: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      R1：\"K/V separation HURTS by 0.3 PPL. This means your framework doesn't naturally handle\n      the K/V asymmetry that RateQuant addresses. RateQuant supports asymmetric K/V allocation\n      (K=2.85, V=2.15) which you listed as a differentiation point — but your own experiment\n      shows separation is worse.\" R2：\"The fact that V heads are all assigned 4-bit under\n      separation suggests V quantization sensitivity is uniform — but you don't analyze WHY,\n      which is the interesting question.\" 在 worst 档下，K/V separation negative 被 reviewer\n      用来论证 framework 不够 flexible，且 RateQuant 在 K/V 处理上更优。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"K/V separation ablation (Qwen2.5-7B)\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Joint K+V MCKP\", 10.91, \"{2:8, 4:100, 8:4}\"]\n          - [\"Separate K/V MCKP\", 11.22, \"K:{2:16,...}, V:all-4bit\"]\n          - [\"Uniform 4-bit\", 15.45, \"all 4-bit\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Negative result。在新 framing 下报告为 \"K/V separation does not improve allocation under\n      our framework\"——honest negative finding 支撑 systematic study 的 credibility。\n\n  - name: \"L0-only heuristic baseline\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_015\"\n    description: \"最简 non-uniform 策略：L0 全 8-bit，其余 uniform 4-bit\"\n    expected_results:\n      status: killed_then_rerun\n      l0_random_mean_ppl: 11.69\n      l0_random_median_ppl: 11.52\n      naive_positional_ppl: 12.23\n      mckp_constrained_ppl: 11.23\n      uniform_4bit_ppl: 15.45\n      mckp_vs_l0_random_median_gap: -5.2%\n    result_rationale: >\n      R3 (最致命)：\"Your L0 heuristic baseline gets PPL 11.52 (median) vs MCKP 10.91 — a gap\n      of only 0.61 PPL. The L0 heuristic requires ZERO profiling (just assign 8-bit to Layer 0),\n      while MCKP requires 65 minutes of GPU time. The marginal benefit of full profiling + MCKP\n      over the trivial L0 heuristic is minimal. Practitioners should just protect Layer 0 and\n      move on.\" R1 补充：\"On Llama, MCKP (8.45) barely beats the L0 heuristic (8.58 naive),\n      and on Mistral, MCKP (7.16) is WORSE than uniform (7.13). The sophisticated optimization\n      adds value only on Qwen, and even there the L0 heuristic gets 80% of the benefit for free.\"\n      在 worst 档下，L0 heuristic 被 reviewer 提升为 \"the real practical recommendation\"——\n      zero-cost, zero-profiling, captures most of the benefit on the one model where benefit exists。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"L0 heuristic vs MCKP across architectures\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Qwen — MCKP\", 10.91, \"65 min profiling\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Qwen — L0 heuristic (median)\", 11.52, \"0 min\", \"80% of MCKP benefit\"]\n          - [\"Qwen — Uniform 4-bit\", 15.45, \"0 min\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Llama — MCKP\", 8.45, \"173 min\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Llama — L0 naive\", 8.58, \"0 min\", \"marginal vs MCKP\"]\n          - [\"Mistral — MCKP\", 7.16, \"~min\", \"WORSE than uniform\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"L0 heuristic as dashed line on PPL comparison bar chart, showing it captures most benefit\"\n    analysis: >\n      L0 heuristic 是 worst 档下 reviewer 手中的核武器：simple, zero-cost, gets most of the\n      benefit。新 framing 必须 honest acknowledge 这一点，并将 MCKP 的 marginal benefit\n      (Qwen: 11.52→10.91) 框定为 \"the gap that motivates profiling when diagnostic recommends\n      it\"。\n\n  - name: \"Greedy + cardinality constraint ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_016\"\n    description: \"RateQuant greedy + max_2bit=k=8 vs constrained MCKP\"\n    expected_results:\n      greedy_constrained_ppl: 11.2312\n      mckp_constrained_ppl: 11.23\n      delta_vs_mckp: 0.0012\n      greedy_unconstrained_ppl: 32.45\n      bit_distribution: \"{2:8, 4:100, 8:4}\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      R3：\"Greedy + constraint = MCKP + constraint (Δ=0.001). This PROVES that MCKP is not a\n      contribution — the constraint alone is sufficient, and any solver (including the simplest\n      greedy) achieves identical results. Your paper presents MCKP as a contribution but your own\n      ablation shows it's irrelevant.\" R2：\"The solver equivalence is not 'surprising' as you\n      claim — it's the expected consequence of a tight constraint that reduces the feasible set\n      to near-singleton. When max_2bit=8 and budget=0.25, there are very few feasible allocations.\n      Any reasonable solver will find the same one.\" R1：\"You've demonstrated that your contribution\n      reduces to a single integer hyperparameter k. This is Appendix-level content, not a paper.\"\n      在 worst 档下，solver equivalence 从 \"surprising finding that the constraint is the\n      contribution\" 翻转为 \"proof that there is no contribution beyond a trivial hyperparameter\"。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Solver equivalence under constraint (Qwen2.5-7B, k=8)\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Greedy unconstrained\", 32.45, \"{2:68, 4:30, 8:4, 16:10}\"]\n          - [\"MCKP unconstrained\", 36.92, \"—\"]\n          - [\"Greedy + k=8\", 11.23, \"{2:8, 4:100, 8:4}\"]\n          - [\"MCKP + k=8\", 11.23, \"{2:8, 4:100, 8:4}\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"四组 bar chart 展示 solver equivalence. Reviewer 标注 'contribution = one hyperparameter k'\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是 worst 档下 reviewer 最强的 single-line attack：\"Your contribution is k=8.\" 新 framing\n      不再将 solver equivalence 作为 surprising finding，而是将其框定为 \"the constrained allocation\n      problem is well-behaved\" 的方法学观察——支撑 \"practitioners need only add one parameter\"\n      的实用结论。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-seed error bars\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_017\"\n    description: \"3 个 calibration seed 的 MCKP PPL mean±std (Qwen2.5-7B)\"\n    expected_results:\n      mckp_mean: 10.9878\n      mckp_std: 0.0648\n      mckp_seeds: [11.02, 10.90, 11.05]\n      uniform_4bit_ppl: 15.45\n      allocation_agreement_3way: 0.902\n      agreement_pairwise_range: [0.911, 0.946]\n    result_rationale: >\n      R2：\"Three seeds is the bare minimum, not rigorous. Standard practice for quantization\n      papers is 5-10 seeds with 95% CI. Your std=0.065 means 95% CI is roughly [10.86, 11.12]\n      — the upper bound is 11.12, still well below uniform 15.45, so the Qwen result holds. But\n      you don't provide multi-seed results for ANY other model. Without error bars on Llama\n      (delta=+0.2%), Yi, Mistral, and Gemma-2, I cannot determine whether their marginal results\n      are signal or noise.\" R1：\"Allocation agreement of 90.2% across 3 seeds means ~10% of heads\n      are assigned differently depending on calibration data. This instability undermines the\n      profiling-based approach — which 10% of heads get 2-bit vs 4-bit is random.\" R3：\"The 90%\n      agreement is particularly concerning for deployment: practitioners can't rely on a specific\n      allocation if it changes with calibration data.\" 在 worst 档下，multi-seed 结果暴露了两个\n      weakness：(1) n=3 seeds 不够，(2) allocation instability 10%。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Multi-seed calibration (Qwen2.5-7B, k=8)\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"Seed 0\", 11.02, \"—\"]\n          - [\"Seed 1\", 10.90, \"—\"]\n          - [\"Seed 2\", 11.05, \"—\"]\n          - [\"Mean ± std\", \"10.99 ± 0.065\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Allocation agreement (3-way)\", \"90.2%\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Error bar plot showing Qwen MCKP stability. Missing: all other models\"\n    analysis: >\n      Multi-seed 在新 framing 下需要扩展：至少 5 seeds on Qwen，3 seeds on 每个额外模型。\n      10% allocation instability 需要 explicitly discuss 并说明为什么 PPL impact 是 minimal\n      (std=0.065)。\n\n  - name: \"Runtime/latency benchmark\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_018\"\n    description: \"端到端推理延迟和吞吐量测量\"\n    expected_results:\n      bf16_throughput: 29.6\n      uniform_4bit_throughput: 23.6\n      mckp_throughput: 21.8\n      bf16_decode_ms: 33.78\n      uniform_4bit_decode_ms: 42.46\n      mckp_decode_ms: 46.09\n      memory_compression: \"4× (both uniform and MCKP)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      R1 (最致命)：\"Mixed-precision MCKP is SLOWER than uniform 4-bit: 21.8 tok/s vs 23.6 tok/s\n      (8% throughput loss), 46.1 ms vs 42.5 ms decode latency (8.5% overhead). You achieve the\n      SAME memory compression (4×) with WORSE latency. For 7/8 models where MCKP doesn't improve\n      PPL, this is a pure loss — worse latency for no quality benefit. Even on Qwen where PPL\n      improves, practitioners must decide whether +29% PPL improvement justifies -8% throughput.\"\n      R2：\"The uniform 4-bit itself is already 20% slower than bf16 — your method adds another\n      8% on top. The memory savings don't translate to speed because your mixed-precision\n      dequantization kernel is not optimized.\" R3：\"The 0.005s solver time is irrelevant — the\n      problem is inference-time overhead from heterogeneous bit-width lookup, which you don't\n      address.\" 在 worst 档下，runtime 结果是 practical deployment value claim 的致命打击。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Inference performance (Qwen2.5-7B, single A100)\"\n        rows:\n          - [\"BF16\", 29.6, 33.78, \"21 MB\"]\n          - [\"Uniform 4-bit\", 23.6, 42.46, \"5.25 MB\"]\n          - [\"MCKP (k=8)\", 21.8, 46.09, \"5.25 MB\"]\n          - [\"MCKP overhead vs uniform\", \"-7.6%\", \"+8.5%\", \"0%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Throughput/latency bar chart. Reviewer 会标注 MCKP overhead 红色\"\n    analysis: >\n      Runtime overhead 是新 framing 下必须直面的 weakness。MCKP 同压缩比下比 uniform 慢 8%，\n      这意味着 Qwen 的 +29% PPL improvement 伴随 8% latency cost。新 framing 应承认这一\n      tradeoff 并将 kernel optimization 列为 future work。对 7/8 无 PPL benefit 的模型，\n      mixed-precision 的 latency overhead 是 pure cost——进一步支撑 \"use diagnostic before\n      profiling\" 的实用建议。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":36476,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"